WHEREAS, the administrative office of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, desires to study the effects of annexation as to the cost of Town services;

WHEREAS, the Town of Clermont also desires to update the maps of the Town of Clermont as to property within the Town limits;

WHEREAS, the Town of Clermont in order to have a comprehensive plan of development within the Town, that balances residential development against commercial development within the Town, and allows the Town to provide services at a reasonable cost, needs a temporary planning period of 190 days in order to develop appropriate Town maps and regulations for the Town;

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, finds that it is appropriate for the Town of Clermont, Georgia to impose a temporary moratorium on annexations;

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, finds that it is appropriate to narrowly tailor this temporary moratorium to only apply to annexations;

